  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v16.2 - New: ResultExceptionHandlerOptions.IncludeErrorCodes gives the built-in answers a code (Request.Invalid, Upstream.Failed, Upstream.Timeout, Server.Error), constants on ResultErrorCodes. Off by default. See CHANGELOG.md.\n\nv16.1 - ToResult, ToActionResult and the enveloped variants throw ArgumentNullException for a null result; httpContext stays optional. See CHANGELOG.md.\n\nv16.0 - Fix: handled 5xx are logged again on .NET 10; 1xx results throw instead of hanging the request; redirects and WithLocation write the Location header. New: 400s from BadHttpRequestException name the field, HttpRequestException is 502 and timeouts 504, public ResultExceptionHandlerOptions.Resolve, AddResultModelStateResponses() for MVC. See CHANGELOG.md.\n\nv15.0 - Breaking (wire): the enveloped success body drops the always-empty \"errors\"/\"fieldErrors\" and is written as ResultEnvelope<T>, which ProducesEnveloped also documents (statusCode as an integer). New: AddResultExceptionHandler() for UseExceptionHandler(), and ToResultAsync/ToEnvelopedResultAsync/ToActionResultAsync/ToEnvelopedActionResultAsync for Task results. See CHANGELOG.md.\n\nv14.0.1 - Fix: MVC validation failures keep their \"errors\" map when Problem Details services are registered; MVC failures apply CustomizeProblemDetails and use normal content negotiation.\n\nv14.0 - Breaking: validation failures use the ASP.NET Core shape (\"errors\" is a field-to-messages map, \"fieldErrors\" removed). Failures go through IProblemDetailsService (CustomizeProblemDetails applies) and always carry instance and traceId. New: \"code\" extension from WithCode, AddResultProblemDetails() for framework errors, ProducesResultProblem(...), and ResultProblemDetails/ResultValidationProblemDetails OpenAPI schemas. See CHANGELOG.md for migration.\n\nv13.3 - ProducesEnveloped<T>() / ProducesEnveloped(): documents the success body ToEnvelopedResult writes (OperationDataResult<T> or OperationResult) for OpenAPI, so API docs and generated clients see the envelope and its data type.\n\nv13.2 - ProducesResultProblems(): one call on a route group documents the Problem Details responses (500, 401/403 for authorized endpoints, 422 for endpoints with a body) for OpenAPI, with no extra package dependency. See CHANGELOG.md for full details.",
